@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@
+# DLSS Neural Rendering (experimental)
+
+Lantern's Windows/Vulkan renderer can run NVIDIA feature 18 immediately before DLSS Super
+Resolution or DLAA:
+
+`scene -> reactive mask -> NR encode/evaluate/ratio resolve -> DLSS SR/DLAA -> post/UI -> present`
+
+The pass uses the engine's real depth and RG16F object/camera motion vectors. It never touches the
+UI. Owned RGBA16F images keep the source, model input, model outputs and resolved result, so the
+game's target is not exposed as an NGX storage output. A feature rebuild waits for submitted work,
+creation and first evaluation cross a GPU submission boundary, and resize/provider/tuning/enable changes
+reset temporal history.
+
+The NR recorder must not call `Scheduler::Finish()` during feature preparation: its caller has
+already acquired the active command buffer. Finishing there submits/replaces that buffer and
+leaves the subsequent NR/SR commands referring to a retired buffer. The recorder waits only for
+previously submitted work and defers rebuilding if its feature was used in the current tick.
+NR owns a separately allocated Vulkan NGX parameter block and never shuts down the shared NGX core.
+Motion uses the same pixel-space `previous - current` convention as SR (`MVecScaleX/Y = +1`).
+
+## Runtime
+
+The proprietary runtime is not distributed. Put `nvngx_dlssnr.dll` in the package's `dlss` folder.
+The launcher and renderer accept the validated x64 DVS production binary by default:
+
+- version: `310.9.16.0`
+- size: `276162560` bytes
+- SHA-256: `CDFA6C1EC784867182164C7836F324F087B5C9F374D0C9FE46F54999FEABF3ED`
+
+Lantern builds the open-source `nvngx.dll_dlssnr.dll` Vulkan caller-gate forwarder into `out`; it
+contains no NVIDIA code. `BB_DLSS_NR_ALLOW_UNKNOWN=1` is an unsupported developer override for
+runtime research.
+
+## Settings
+
+`dlss_nr=1` enables the pass (default off). `dlss_nr_height` selects its real render height while DLSS SR is in
+use; width follows the output aspect ratio and both dimensions are multiples of four. Native
+height is saved as `0`; AA/DLAA always renders at output size and preserves the saved lower choice. Tuning keys are
+`dlss_nr_preset`, `dlss_nr_intensity`, `dlss_nr_style`, `dlss_nr_local_structure`,
+`dlss_nr_local_tone`, `dlss_nr_skin_structure`, `dlss_nr_auto_mask`, and `dlss_nr_white_point`.
+
+Keep automatic masking enabled (default `1`). With no explicit control mask and the default skin
+strength, the validated runtime returns identical RGB when automatic masking is disabled; this
+was verified by same-frame proxy/model GPU readback. It still incurs model cost. The runtime's
+automatic mask does not require Streamline material tags. Core strengths default to `1.0`, white
+point to its minimum `0.125`, skin structure to `-1`, and style/preset to `0`. Tuning is editable
+while NR is off. White point is saved with three decimal places so `0.125` round-trips exactly.
+Existing saved values are not migrated.
+The status GPU time comes from a nonblocking four-slot timestamp ring, read after completion.
+
+`dlss_nr_passes` selects 1 (default), 2 or 3 chained evaluations. Each pass owns a separate
+feature/history and output image; the next consumes the previous result with the same depth and
+motion. Color encoding happens once and the final result is composed once against the original.
+Changing the count rebuilds safely and resets all histories. GPU time covers the entire chain;
+more passes increase model cost and memory use, and are not guaranteed to look better.
+
+`dlss_nr_customize_passes=1` enables independent style, intensity, local structure, local tone and
+skin structure for passes 2 and 3. The overlay puts the checkbox beside the pass selector and
+shows a section for each enabled extra pass. Pass 1 uses the main controls. Keys are
+`dlss_nr_pass2_intensity`, `dlss_nr_pass2_local_structure`, `dlss_nr_pass2_local_tone`,
+`dlss_nr_pass2_skin_structure` (and the same `pass3_` keys). While customization is off,
+extra passes inherit the main values; saved overrides are retained for re-enabling it.
+`dlss_nr_pass2_style` and `dlss_nr_pass3_style` select -1 (Use main style, default), 0 (Standard),
+1 (Natural), or 2 (Cinematic). The inherited default preserves the look of older custom profiles.
+Pass 1 uses the main `dlss_nr_style`. Turning customization off ignores, but retains, overrides.
+The effective style is supplied to both feature creation and evaluation; changing an active
+pass's style triggers the same safe feature rebuild/history reset as its numeric tuning.
+Only effective settings for active passes enter the feature rebuild key. White point, preset,
+and automatic mask remain shared; per-pass white point would require decode/re-encode
+between layers rather than the current encode-once chain.
+
+All overlay sliders and both launchers' shared slider rows have a circular reset arrow and
+a default-value tooltip. Reset changes only the associated value, saves normally, and follows
+the existing renderer rebuild/history-reset rules. Extra-pass numeric defaults are 1,1,1,-1.
+
+NR presets are limited to Default/1/2/3 and styles to Standard/Natural/Cinematic, matching the
+community-tested OptiScaler menu. These are undocumented hints, not strength levels: the runtime
+may alias presets. Style names are community labels rather than NVIDIA metadata.
+
+Any missing/invalid runtime, unsupported GPU, feature creation, or evaluation failure bypasses NR
+only. Ordinary DLSS and the existing renderer remain available without a restart.
+
+## Developer diagnostics
+
+These are disabled unless explicitly requested through the environment:
+
+- `BB_DLSS_NR_DEBUG=1`: four vertical regions (source, decoded proxy, decoded model, composition),
+  marked red/green/blue/yellow across the top and separated by magenta dividers.
+- `BB_DLSS_NR_CAPTURE=<directory>`: save original, proxy, every `model-passN`, and final resolve
+  RGBA16F buffers from one frame after 120 evaluations. Each rebuild gets a separate numbered
+  directory including dimensions and pass count. `size.txt` gives dimensions and `settings.txt`
+  records HDR/white point/model settings. Captures are written after GPU completion. Compare
+  each model against the previous model, then reproduce the ratio resolve against the same
+  original/proxy to distinguish model convergence from composition suppressing differences.
+- `BB_DLSS_NR_CONTROL=<file>`: live research controls, four whitespace-separated values:
+  `case_id motion_scale auto_mask reset`. A changed case id resets history and rearms the capture.
+  `auto_mask` and `reset` use `-1` for normal settings, `0/1` to override. Production motion is `+1`.
+
+`hdr-native-shader-test --nr` checks the production shader's HDR/LDR identity resolve (including
+near-black values and alpha) and verifies a changed model actually changes the resolved image.
